claimed: intent-live-provider — close the claim I shipped unmeasured: the spec says Structured.cut stops generation at the closing brace so a classification costs the answer, and calls that reasoned about rather than measured. Wire the streaming call to the classify prompt and put a number on it: tokens consumed with the early stop against tokens generated without it, on the same fixture messages. If the saving is small the spec loses a sentence it has not earned; if it is large the cheap arm from the field-order decision becomes worth revisiting, since that trade was priced in characters of prose and not in tokens actually paid for.
